  "description": "Simply, the lightest, stiffest, fastest fat bikes available. In 2013, we introduced the 9:ZERO:7 Whiteout Carbon that changed it all. With a runner up finish in 2014 and a win in the 2015 Fat Bike Birkie (the largest fat bike race in the world), the 9:ZERO:7 Whiteout Carbon set the bar in high performance fat bikes. Yet, we knew we could still do better. So last year, we introduced our 9:ZERO:7 Whiteout Carbon Team Edition frame utilizing Toray T1000 Carbon to bring the frame weight down to a mere 1250 grams. The NEW 9:ZERO:7 Whiteout Team Edition saw instant success by once again taking the top step of the podium at the 2016 Fat Bike Birkie. This frame combined with our 9:ZERO:7 Storm 80mm Rims and SRAM's New XX1 Eagle drivetrain make this bike the gold standard in high performance fat bikes ready for #allconditions.",
